.TH NOSTR-HOME-FUSE 8 "2026-09-25" "nostr-homed 0.3" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
nostr-home-fuse \- read-only portable-home FUSE overlay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nostr-home-fuse
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nostr-home-fuse
mounts the current portable-home snapshot at
.I $HOME/Portable
(or
.BR $NH_FUSE_MOUNTPOINT )
as a read-only FUSE3 filesystem. The tree is served from the on-disk
snapshot the syncd maintains under
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed ,
with per-file chunks decrypted on demand. Writes are refused with
.BR EROFS ;
the writable path is the real home, published back by
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8).
.PP
The mount is per-user and runs under
.B systemd \-\-user
via
.IR nostr-home-fuse.service .
It requires a running
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8)
to produce and rotate snapshots.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NH_FUSE_MOUNTPOINT
Mountpoint override. Default:
.IR $HOME/Portable .
The directory is created (mode 0700) if it does not exist.
.TP
.B NH_FUSE_STATE_DIR
Override the snapshot state directory. Default:
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed .
.TP
.B NH_FUSE_HOME
Override
.I $HOME
for the tier-0 pread path (tests only).
.TP
.B NH_FUSE_STATUS_DIR
Override
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nostr-homed
for the status writer.
.TP
.B NH_FUSE_CHUNK_SIZE
Force a chunk size (bytes). Live-acceptance rigs only; production reads
the manifest.
.TP
.B NH_FUSE_SEED_FILE
Override the broker seed drop path. Default same as
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8).
.TP
.B NH_FUSE_SEED_HEX
Inline seed for headless tests. Ignored unless the source tree was built
with the test harness.
.TP
.B NH_FUSE_NO_LOOP
When set to 1, skip
.BR fuse_loop (3):
mount, notify readiness, exit. For lifecycle tests.
.TP
.B NH_FUSE_TEST_HARNESS
When set to 1, skip the actual
.B fuse_mount
call \(em runs table + reload plumbing against an empty mount surface. For
CI without /dev/fuse.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_PORTHOME_FUSE_NO_INOTIFY
When set to 1, disable the inotify-based snapshot reloader and fall back
to polling. Escape hatch for kernels where inotify on the state directory
is unreliable.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_NOTIFY
When set to 0, disable D-Bus notifications back to syncd on reload.
Diagnostic use.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/Portable
Default mountpoint.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed/snapshots/
Snapshot store maintained by
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8).
.TP
.I /run/nostr-auth/session/<uid>/home_seed
Broker seed drop \(em same source as syncd. Read once, mlocked.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nostr-homed/porthome-fuse-status.json
Per-mount status file (mounted state, current pointer id, reload
generation).
.SH EXIT CODES
.RS
.TP 4
.B 0
Clean unmount.
.TP 4
.B 3
State directory or $HOME not resolvable.
.TP 4
.B 6
Mountpoint creation failure.
.RE
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Clean unmount and exit.
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Force snapshot reload.
.SH SECURITY
Runs as the login user; sets
.B RLIMIT_CORE
to 0 before touching the seed; refuses to run as root; enforces
.B allow_other=no
on the mount so only the owning uid can read it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8),
.BR nostr-home-status (1),
.BR nostr-homed-provision (1),
.BR fuse (8)
